\subsection{Cross-Model Validation}
\label{sec:cross-model}

Table~\ref{tab:cross-model} replicates full S1 with Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct and Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3 under identical prompts and evaluation.
Mistral serves as a third zero-shot verification point; composability evaluation (\S\ref{sec:composability}) uses LoRA, available only for Qwen and Llama.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{3.4pt}
\resizebox{\columnwidth}{!}{%
\begin{tabular}{@{}ll rrrr r@{}}
\toprule
& & \multicolumn{4}{c}{\textbf{Violation Rates (\%)}}
& \textbf{R-F1} \\
\cmidrule(lr){3-6} \cmidrule(l){7-7}
\textbf{Dataset} & \textbf{Model}
  & DR\,$\downarrow$ & RV\,$\downarrow$ & ET\,$\downarrow$ & CF
  & $\uparrow$ \\
\midrule
\multirow{6}{*}{SciERC}
  & Qwen (U)    & 15.37 & 1.39  & 0.40 & 0.08 & 8.23 \\
  & Qwen (S1)   &  0.93 & 0     & 0    & 9.90 & 8.36 \\
  \cmidrule(l){2-7}
  & Llama (U)   & 13.34 & 0.55  & 0    & 0.24 & 2.68 \\
  & Llama (S1)  &  0.08 & 0     & 0    & 6.56 & 2.54 \\
  \cmidrule(l){2-7}
  & Mistral (U) & 56.94 & 0     & 1.50 & 56.87$^\dagger$ & 3.66 \\
  & Mistral (S1)& 13.40 & 0     & 0    & 1.27  & 3.67 \\
\midrule
\multirow{6}{*}{DocRED}
  & Qwen (U)    & 18.46 & 29.66 & 2.48 & 0.10 & 7.74 \\
  & Qwen (S1)   & 10.21 &  0.03 & 0    & 2.57 & 8.23 \\
  \cmidrule(l){2-7}
  & Llama (U)   & 26.07 & 16.03 & 0.13 & 0.17 & 5.98 \\
  & Llama (S1)  &  2.55 &  0    & 0    & 12.02& 6.27 \\
  \cmidrule(l){2-7}
  & Mistral (U) & 57.42 & 42.35 & 7.58 & 24.78 & 4.34 \\
  & Mistral (S1)& 33.20 &  0    & 0    & 0.19  & 5.52 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}}%
\caption{Three-model zero-shot validation. U: unconstrained; S1: full two-layer.
Parse failures: Llama DocRED 9.1\%; others $\leq$1.1\%.
$^\dagger$Mistral: poor zero-shot calibration causes pervasive type inconsistencies.
F1 $\times$100.}
\label{tab:cross-model}
\end{table}

% exp_ids: phase2_scierc_full_s1, llama_scierc_full_s1, phase2_docred_full_s1, llama_docred_full_s1, mistral_scierc, mistral_docred
\paragraph{Results.}
RV and ET are eliminated ($\leq$0.03\%) for all models on both datasets.
DR drops 76--99\% on SciERC and 42--90\% on DocRED; R-F1 improves in five of six settings (DocRED: Qwen $+$0.50\,pp, $p{<}0.001$; Llama $+$0.29\,pp, $p{=}0.013$).
Cross-model DR asymmetry reflects baseline RV: Llama's lower RV (16.03\% vs.\ 29.66\%) limits latent violation surfacing, yielding 2.55\% residual DR vs.\ 10.21\%.
CF direction depends on baseline calibration: S1 introduces CF for calibrated models (up to 12.02\%; \S\ref{sec:discussion}), while reducing CF for poorly-calibrated Mistral (56.87\%\,$\to$\,1.27\%).

